  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education amidst Crisis: Safe schools for learners in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is going to be implemented in Greater Pibor Administrative Area (GPAA) and the main actions under this project are improving access to education through rehabilitating existing learning spaces and construction of new ones, equipping school facilities with age appropriate furniture and scholastic materials, addressing social and economic barriers  to improve enrolment and retention, construction and maintenance of water facilities in learning spaces, training teachers for improved quality education, etc. Oxfam will implement this project in GPAA with local implementing partner, Church and Development. The project beneficiaries are estimated as 7390 of which 43.5% will be female.</narrative>
  </description>
